      "waste_details": [
        {
          "reason_for_no_provision": "The application relates to an existing self-contained basement flat within an established three-storey Victorian terraced building. No external waste or recycling storage exists for any flat in the building; waste is stored internally and presented at the kerbside for collection, in common with other properties in the terrace.  This application creates no new residential units and generates no additional waste storage demand. It comprises the replacement of windows and doors within existing structural openings and the retention of an existing air-conditioning installation. No change to waste storage arrangements is proposed or required.  The building has no side access, forecourt or communal area capable of accommodating external bin storage. Any new external storage would be within the front lightwell or private rear garden, would be visible in the street scene or would require alteration to the setting of a building within the Oxford Road Conservation Area, and is not proportionate to a proposal of this limited scale.",
